These four native input classes derive from Forge, not from our application's
rules implementation. Original upstream copyright and license comments are
retained. Our changes add input-presentation/provenance notifications and prevent
stale queued mana callbacks from interacting with a replacement prompt. The
2026-11-06 InputProxy change also publishes completed synchronous stack-target
clicks through the same native presentation fence, without changing other
ability-click paths. The
modified sources identify their changes. InputPayMana's original source has no
file header; its modified copy explicitly credits Forge and identifies GPL3+.

LICENSE is the unchanged upstream forge-gui module license. The Forge root
license is also retained at ../LICENSE. Keep the notices and source headers.
The application's root Apache license does not override these GPL-licensed files.

UPSTREAM-SHA256.json identifies the exact upstream preimages used to make the
patches. Apply either patches/native-coupled.patch or the four individual patches,
not both. Do not compile another copy of these FQNs from an upstream source tree
in the same source batch; the build's explicit source list selects these copies.

The adjacent adapter/helper and unit sources are separately marked
GPL-3.0-or-later. Generated private game traces, dependencies, compiled engine
binaries and card programs are not distributed in this checkpoint. This is a
local process prototype, not a completed application migration.
